"The link opens the demo with <strong>Two stars</strong> pressed (at the top, next to <strong>Star and planet</strong>), playing the setup <strong>Sun and red dwarf</strong>. The setups are listed under <strong>Systems</strong> in the panel on the right.",
"<strong>Part {#}. Weigh four pairs.</strong> Press the setup <strong>Seesaw: {#} and {#} suns</strong>. It opens in the <strong>Visual</strong> view: watch the two stars go around for a few orbits, and note which star is on the bigger circle and which moves faster. Press <strong>Record reading</strong> (in the Readings section of the panel). Then press <strong>Alpha Centauri A and B</strong>, <strong>Spectroscopic pair</strong> and <strong>Sun and red dwarf</strong> in turn, and press <strong>Record reading</strong> after each. That makes four readings. Press <strong>Export to worksheet</strong>: they go into Table {#}, with the separation \\(a\\), the period \\(P\\) in years, and each star’s distance from the center of mass, \\(a_1\\) and \\(a_2\\).",
